The primary goal of the design structure was to keep everything as modular and reusable as possible. almost all the coupling is loose, so that the master/child relationships can theoretically be any classes. 
The buttons and button handler were probably the most difficult parts. It took a lot of tinkering to allow the buttons to issue commands when pressed, but still keep the loose coupling. 
The messiest part of the code and the place that needs improvement the most is the get from files library. Currently, it does not have great modularity. Every time I want something, 
I have to create a new function that calls the abstract get_from_line_by_keyword() function. It works, it just gets really messy really fast. 
